<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>

    <!--
        Quill ships one copy of each raster icon, at xxxhdpi, and lets Android downsample.

        Lint wants five copies — hdpi through xxxhdpi — and says so once per missing bucket.
        That is the right advice for an icon set authored per density. Ours is not: these are
        single high-resolution exports from an icon pack, drawn at 18-40dp, and downsampling from
        one 4x source is visually indistinguishable from a hand-tuned 2x asset at those sizes.
        Five copies of 41 icons would be 205 files and roughly 2 MB to maintain by hand.

        Suppressed here rather than left as a warning, because the obvious way to "fix" it is to
        generate the other four buckets, and that would be a mistake made on lint's authority.

        The real fix is to convert these to vector drawables, at which point the whole question
        disappears — see the drawable convention in memory/note.md.
    -->
    <issue id="IconDensities" severity="ignore" />

</lint>
